---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';

const description =
  'What counts as a neolab, how this map encodes valuation, lineage, geography, and research area, and what the data does and does not claim.';
---

<Layout title="Neolabs.fyi | About" description={description} path="/about">
  <article class="prose">
    <h1>What's a neolab?</h1>
    <p>
      An AI research, infrastructure, or product lab or company, typically founded by researchers
      hailing from incumbent labs, professors, or post-economic founders. They're usually
      pre-product-market-fit and sub-revenue-scale, yet are capable of raising at unicorn-plus
      valuations due to strong investor appetite.
    </p>

    <h2>Why are certain labs missing?</h2>
    <p>The neolab definition excludes labs already at revenue scale.</p>
    <details class="about-exclusions">
      <summary>See excluded labs</summary>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>OpenAI</strong> — Revenue scale</li>
        <li><strong>Anthropic</strong> — Revenue scale</li>
        <li><strong>Google DeepMind</strong> — Revenue scale</li>
        <li><strong>xAI</strong> — Revenue scale</li>
        <li><strong>Roze</strong> — Still being planned</li>
        <li><strong>Z.ai</strong> — Revenue scale</li>
        <li><strong>DeepSeek</strong> — Revenue scale</li>
        <li><strong>Moonshot AI</strong> — Revenue scale</li>
        <li><strong>MiniMax</strong> — Revenue scale</li>
        <li><strong>AgiBot</strong> — Revenue scale</li>
        <li><strong>Prime Intellect</strong> — Revenue scale</li>
        <li><strong>Mistral</strong> — Revenue scale</li>
        <li><strong>Cohere</strong> — Revenue scale</li>
        <li><strong>Runway</strong> — Revenue scale</li>
        <li><strong>Black Forest Labs</strong> — Revenue scale</li>
      </ul>
    </details>

    <h2>What am I looking at?</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Research area</strong> — neolabs clustered by their primary research focus.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Lineage</strong> — neolabs wired to the organizations their founders came from.
      </li>
      <li><strong>Geography</strong> — where neolabs are primarily headquartered.</li>
      <li>
        <strong>Valuation</strong> — a single cluster of all neolabs, with nodes scaled to their
        valuations.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Table</strong> — the same neolabs as a sortable table. It reads the same filters as
        the map, so a search or a filter set carries between them.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Caveats</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Valuations are messy, and many are likely inaccurate or need better fact-checking.</li>
      <li>
        Headquarters, founder lists, and founder backgrounds may be inaccurate or missing
        information.
      </li>
      <li>
        Many neolabs are actively exploring multiple research areas and don't fit cleanly into a
        single category.
      </li>
    </ul>
  </article>
</Layout>
